From 701fb1cbb9a827b86edd4d07af0ba1374f4a4665 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alexdremov <dremov.me@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:01:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 142/202] Gui: Guard task dialog references with QPointer
 against deferred deletion

TaskInfo stored raw pointers to the task panel, dialog and control
widget. Since removal is deferred via deleteLater(), the actual
destruction happens at an arbitrary later point - and FreeCAD pumps
nested event loops in many places (progress sequencer during
recomputes, modal dialogs), so the deferred deletion can flush while
TaskView::accept()/reject()/clicked() are still using the pointers.
This was observed as a use-after-free crash inside the guard-property
reset right after TaskDialog::reject() returned (SIGSEGV reading
reused heap memory at address 0x4, frame TaskView::reject+232), and
as crashes dispatching events through already-destroyed widgets.

Make TaskInfo hold QPointer members so destruction - whenever it
happens - is detectable, and check the pointers:
- accept()/reject(): bail out cleanly when the dialog died during its
  own accept()/reject(), instead of resetting the guard property on a
  corpse; also guard the initial hide() and the restore show(). Both
  methods delegate to a shared acceptOrReject() so the paired handling
  cannot drift; the destruction warning names the method via fmt
- removeDialog(): handle entries whose dialog is already gone (erase
  the stale entry, dispose of leftover widgets) and guard the widget
  cleanup
- clicked()/helpRequested()/setShownTaskInfo()/auto-close slots/
  transactionChangeOnDocument (re-locate entry after onUndo()/onRedo() may
  have pumped events)/contextual panel handling/action style helpers:
  guard every dereference

Assisted-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (Z.ai)
